Valid JS lookahead pattern built at run time after a tool call (outside RE2).
-- script.js --
const q = mcp.search.query({});
const re = new RegExp("\\b" + q.term + "(?!-draft)\\b", "gi");
return q.docs.filter(d => re.test(d));
-- tools.json --
{
  "search.query": {
    "term": "plan",
    "docs": [
      "plan-draft",
      "the plan",
      "Plan B",
      "planet"
    ]
  }
}
-- divergence --
Runtime-built regex outside RE2 after a tool call: native reports ErrRuntimeUnsupported and cannot fall back once effects happened (compile.go ErrRuntimeUnsupported contract).
